   ",", "\<\"TotalEnergyUncertainty\"\>", ",", "\<\"WavefunctionP\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"WavefunctionX\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.000412842855994*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[9]=",
 CellID->736185335,ExpressionUUID->"b22aa950-e40a-4940-9320-026522b392f1"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Mathematical Definitions", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998762043417219*^9, 3.998762055137306*^9}, {
  3.9987652888694277`*^9, 3.998765292744068*^9}},
 CellID->534936632,ExpressionUUID->"7bcc005f-d0af-4784-adab-9ac7a998124a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Generalized Complex-Valued Gaussian Wavepacket (GWP)", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998825563968564*^9, 3.99882557614466*^9}},
 CellID->210064920,ExpressionUUID->"06d54978-4acd-4a22-9d77-43686d9a5643"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The notation and parameterization utilized throughout the GWPTools \
framework are based strictly on the formalism presented in Chapter 3 of David \
Tannor's ",
 StyleBox["Introduction to Quantum Mechanics: A Time-Dependent Perspective",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->317772612,ExpressionUUID->"809cdfb4-7496-4128-9245-d96a2de056d8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
The mathematical form of a generalized, complex-valued Gaussian wavepacket in \
one spatial dimension is defined as:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->12459795,ExpressionUUID->"dd8a5d12-2357-4aa3-bfb1-9a83b7130d16"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalPsi]", "(", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], ")"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"N", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "t"], "(", 
         RowBox[{"x", "-", 
          SubscriptBox["x", "t"]}], ")"}], "2"]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox["\[ImaginaryI]", "\[HBar]"], " ", 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["p", "t"], "(", 
        RowBox[{"x", "-", 
         SubscriptBox["x", "t"]}], ")"}]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox["\[ImaginaryI]", "\[HBar]"], " ", 
       SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", "t"]}]}]]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellMargins->{{30, Inherited}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998824990424766*^9, 3.998825044480611*^9}, 
   3.998828141462399*^9},
 FontSize->16,
 CellID->839912931,ExpressionUUID->"5cdcbef1-6579-469e-8d36-752d4a1bd613"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "x", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f0138f6a-b67f-42a2-9f29-ce03c4288c7a"],
 " is the spatial coordinate, \[HBar] is the reduced Planck constant, and the \
wavepacket is completely characterized by four continuously evolving \
parameters: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\alpha_t", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0d01be91-8a92-421a-b6b5-627ecf06b904"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "x_t", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "be9e7257-5a27-4dde-a7e4-49055f6e70ea"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "p_t", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ccd1134a-ac52-4f3e-8e38-8510a7e42bb0"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\gamma_t", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ae835678-68ff-41e5-af74-cd45658f6a3c"],
 ". In this representation, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "x_t", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c79bdaeb-1a6b-44df-9505-91d45cb7d494"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "p_t", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5e353581-f9dc-4a48-a599-7337daa7ca24"],
 " are strictly real-valued quantities, representing the exact center-of-mass \
position and momentum expectation values."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998825070716321*^9, 3.9988251801538553`*^9}, {
   3.99882815112083*^9, 3.9988281546987123`*^9}, 3.998828188789846*^9, {
   3.998828273297927*^9, 3.998828273963642*^9}, {3.998829565726853*^9, 
   3.9988296290669613`*^9}},
 CellID->1137541171,ExpressionUUID->"02245cca-e6f2-4fcb-b3c7-3bdde9330c14"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The complex shape parameter, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\alpha_t", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "95009880-eea8-4f43-ab1d-e72cdadf75b0"],
 ", completely characterizes the phase-space uncertainty bounds of the state. \
Its real part ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"Re", "(", 
         SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"]], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "\\text{Re}(\\alpha_t)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e0c619da-9e07-4a23-b163-1a4cb11528a9"],
 " governs the spatial variance, while its imaginary part ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"Im", "(", 
         SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"]], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "\\text{Im}(\\alpha_t)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0316d23b-724c-4e14-a1a3-ce4d1c660d5f"],
 " dictates the position-momentum correlation, commonly referred to as the \
momentum \"chirp.\" Similarly, the complex phase parameter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\gamma_t", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cbde6e58-4175-4da7-8b0a-b3f42f20f91a"],
 " captures the global phase evolution. Its real component accumulates both \
the classical action and the quantum phase shift induced by wavepacket \
spreading (analogous to the Gouy phase in optics), while its imaginary \
component ensures proper time-dependent normalization."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998825244900981*^9, 3.9988252737038717`*^9}, {
  3.998825421991647*^9, 3.998825476233966*^9}, {3.998828382958246*^9, 
  3.998828414425962*^9}},
 CellID->1886702625,ExpressionUUID->"f93d667d-de03-4c51-ac2c-926ecaa21ce8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The normalization constant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["N", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "N", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8b8e9d90-3bc0-4ede-bb87-d47e5500c513"],
 " is purely real-valued and independent of time for quadratic systems, given \
by:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9988252949386387`*^9, {3.998825508472007*^9, 3.9988255125277452`*^9}},
 CellID->2008084127,ExpressionUUID->"8491d429-b9e3-44ef-80e1-438f082d5bef"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{"N", " ", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox["2", "\[Pi]"], 
       RowBox[{"Re", "(", 
        SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "0"], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["1", "\[HBar]"], 
      RowBox[{"Im", "(", 
       SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", "0"], ")"}]}]]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellMargins->{{30, Inherited}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998824990424766*^9, 3.998825044480611*^9}, {
  3.9988252078019867`*^9, 3.998825224201375*^9}, {3.998825304894185*^9, 
  3.998825337866495*^9}, {3.998828423028841*^9, 3.998828433093205*^9}},
 FontSize->16,
 CellID->1667664980,ExpressionUUID->"852c7f8b-a1f2-42f6-8a06-f87823c306e3"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["External Potentials & Time Evolution", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998825586056041*^9, 3.9988255972629747`*^9}},
 CellID->293716617,ExpressionUUID->"160e9129-9c09-4563-9cac-7a525f4ce9fa"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
The dynamical evolution of the wavepacket is governed by an external \
potential energy field, $V(x,t)$, which is locally approximated or exactly \
defined as a polynomial up to second order in the spatial coordinate:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1805928099,ExpressionUUID->"97d2e570-d60d-4d47-8ede-91b9a4b465d7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"V", "(", 
    RowBox[{"x", ",", "t"}], ")"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["V", "0"], "(", "t", ")"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["V", "1"], "(", "t", ")"}], "x"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["V", "2"], "(", "t", ")"}], 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}]}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormulaNumbered",
 CellMargins->{{30, Inherited}, {Inherited, Inherited}},
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998824990424766*^9, 3.998825044480611*^9}, {
  3.9988252078019867`*^9, 3.998825224201375*^9}, {3.998825304894185*^9, 
  3.998825337866495*^9}, {3.998825613781633*^9, 3.998825630278976*^9}},
 FontSize->16,
 CellID->1847176842,ExpressionUUID->"dfd0957d-eaad-48fb-a86a-4bbcbe413d5e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
A foundational property of this mathematical framework is that any \
generalized Gaussian wavepacket propagating in a strictly quadratic potential \
will exactly preserve its Gaussian functional form for all time.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->248763645,ExpressionUUID->"110587cc-5d0a-4801-a753-639b06110667"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The framework natively supports time-dependent coefficients for the \
potential. In the current version, explicit time-dependence is \
comprehensively supported for the external forcing term, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["V", "TI"], "1"], "(", 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "V_1(t)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "478eb979-ff08-4f76-86d1-953dc1940ced"],
 ", permitting linear and sinusoidal dynamic driving forces. Implementations \
featuring arbitrary time-dependent shifts to the reference energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["V", "TI"], "0"], "(", 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "V_0(t)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ce02bdf1-877c-40ef-8800-580cecd89ef9"],
 " or the harmonic curvature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["V", "TI"], "2"], "(", 
         StyleBox["t", "TI"], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "V_2(t)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2910c986-9139-4c2a-b123-67ae24223ddc"],
 " are designated for future development."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998825678292264*^9, 3.998825717153812*^9}},
 CellID->1967404453,ExpressionUUID->"ac2560f4-39c2-4d8b-bc7f-d81ccd327d5b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Under this quadratic evolution, the time-dependent wavepacket is \
continuously characterized by the parameters defined above. These variables (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\alpha_t", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3cdef17d-4cae-4969-8275-75690c940403"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "x_t", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2b5ed65a-d42e-4fb2-aa73-92df8f348c56"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "p_t", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a2bae294-9687-45d9-88af-3166a861d17b"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\gamma_t", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3e4f611c-6f37-489e-8931-bdbd54cc90ec"],
 ") are uniquely determined at any time ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "t", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b9829294-bc1f-4ca8-9da2-503fa247f489"],
 " by their initial values (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "0"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "\\alpha_0", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "80d8c701-fe10-49ba-9f23-0d855d950f2a"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "0"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "x_0", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "441baa2d-3aae-4cf8-aa19-1a7035005bc2"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["p", "TI"], "0"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "p_0", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "02f39a95-89f6-40bf-8462-3be8a080f661"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["\[Gamma]", "0"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "\\gamma_0", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "06b57bab-8581-4f78-97fe-46a060abebc5"],
 ") and the instantaneous coefficients of the potential energy field. The GWP \
constructor accepts these initial values as input arguments to instantiate a \
specific physical state. By querying the resulting dynamic GWPObject, the \
internal code automatically evaluates these underlying parameters to \
construct exact time-dependent probabilities, expectation values, and \
wavefunctions."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998828531320161*^9, 3.998828539568845*^9}, {
   3.99882969656952*^9, 3.99882970342386*^9}, 3.998829893035733*^9, {
   3.9988299257267733`*^9, 3.9988299329044113`*^9}, 3.998830051118599*^9},
 CellID->739880842,ExpressionUUID->"482b1c2e-bed4-42e0-a04b-938ce881b4d2"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Representations & Observables", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998827526224886*^9, 3.9988275328813877`*^9}},
 CellID->1049281124,ExpressionUUID->"7bf43387-af81-49f9-b202-0832700bd74c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A primary advantage of the generalized Gaussian framework is that the \
wavepacket maintains a closed-form, exact analytical representation across \
multiple domains. The GWPTools package natively supports the momentum-space \
representation, evaluating the momentum-space wavefunction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox["\[CapitalPsi]", "~"], "(", 
         RowBox[{
           StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", 
           StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "\\tilde{\\Psi}(p, t)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ce249ef4-a495-4c8a-b64c-e074e134156d"],
 " and density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox["\[Rho]", "~"], "(", 
         RowBox[{
           StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", 
           StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "\\tilde{\\rho}(p, t)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8ceb0a2d-fecd-4b0b-bf3d-9c640ac9b87e"],
 " directly from the core parameters without relying on numerical Fourier \
transforms."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.99882758636511*^9, 3.998827601902631*^9}, {
   3.9988300605236588`*^9, 3.998830062875353*^9}, 3.998843158391768*^9},
 CellID->465578820,ExpressionUUID->"19a8f4a7-8e83-4e87-be1e-714bb99db599"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Because the underlying probability densities are Gaussian, exact algebraic \
solutions exist for the expectation values of physical operators. The \
internal code utilizes recursive algorithms to analytically evaluate \
arbitrary-order position moments ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "\\langle \\hat{x}^n \\rangle", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3817abdb-6614-4b77-bab7-ed0bc1faa59d"],
 ", momentum moments ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "\\langle \\hat{p}^n \\rangle", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0ec3d6c2-c948-40d0-a686-198aec170ceb"],
 ", and position-momentum cross-products ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
         RowBox[{
           SuperscriptBox[
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
            StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
           SuperscriptBox[
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], 
            StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\langle \\hat{x}^m \\hat{p}^n \\rangle", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "514c3040-15e2-4ef0-97bc-c98a3f6abea7"],
 ". This permits the exact extraction of higher-order \
observables\[LongDash]including kinetic, potential, and total energy moments \
up to the fourth order\[LongDash]completely bypassing the computational \
overhead and accuracy limits of numerical spatial quadrature."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998827610151731*^9, 3.998827650003853*^9}, 
   3.998829782538138*^9, {3.998830119110178*^9, 3.998830122840958*^9}},
 CellID->1700301719,ExpressionUUID->"61017321-62d3-4f00-876c-c64b98185f6b"],

Cell["\<\
Finally, integrating the probability densities yields closed-form Cumulative \
Distribution Functions (CDFs). The package leverages these analytical CDFs to \
instantly evaluate interval probabilities across position space, momentum \
space, and the classical energy domain.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->406100604,ExpressionUUID->"1459d661-6c95-4aec-936b-6b708c58753e"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["GWP & GWPObject Introspection Interface", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998765370112008*^9, 3.998765373613098*^9}, {
   3.998767076089282*^9, 3.9987670993286333`*^9}, 3.9988349970902567`*^9},
 CellID->658646242,ExpressionUUID->"f9b57ea5-3daa-4a2a-968d-537c2c3c5c72"],

Cell["\<\
The GWPTools package employs a factory pattern for wavepacket construction. \
As defined by its primary usage statement, GWP[type][parameters, options] \
returns a GWPObject representing a Gaussian wavepacket with the specified \
type, parameters, and options. The foundational supported type is \"1D\", \
representing a generalized Gaussian wavepacket in one spatial dimension.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.998834215740806*^9, 3.998835253334662*^9},
 CellID->1519054963,ExpressionUUID->"3ebb0731-0929-445f-bc72-269b02836353"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
List the currently available wavepacket types. Only the \"1D\" type is \
available by default.\
\>", "MathCaption",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9988350383364573`*^9, 3.998835053300891*^9}, {
  3.998835271268498*^9, 3.998835280733871*^9}},
